## 7. Errors, Bottlenecks and Resolutions

| # | Symptom / Error | Root cause | Resolution |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Near-perfect BLEU (implausible) | Target sentence embedded in LLM prompt | Instruction-only prompt; remove ICL/derangement |
| 2 | `CUDA out of memory` at model load | mt0-xl fp32 ≈15.1 GiB > 15.57 GiB usable | Load backbone in bf16 (~7.4 GiB) |
| 3 | Test-time OOM (`Tried to allocate 2 MiB ... 3.25 MiB free`) | Checkpoint saved from GPU tensors + generation KV cache | `map_location="cpu"`; `empty_cache()`; best-ckpt reload; `--test-batch-size 1`; `expandable_segments:True` |
| 4 | CTC had no effect | CPU `LongTensor` targets vs GPU logits; `zero_infinity=False`; no invalid filtering | Move targets to device/dtype; `zero_infinity=True`; filter invalid; guard + warning |
| 5 | DDP incompatibility with gradient checkpointing | Reentrant checkpointing | `use_reentrant: False` |
| 6 | Positional encoding applied along batch axis | `(B,T,C)` fed to encoder expecting `(T,B,C)` | Permute before/after `pos_enc` (`modules/ff.py`) |
| 7 | Crash when pose absent | Unconditional pose init | Guard pose loading on `include_pose` |
| 8 | `ModuleNotFoundError: utils.translate_en` | New file not uploaded to server | Upload the new module |
| 9 | Google Translate `TooManyRequests` (429) on first call | Datacenter IP throttled by Google | MyMemory fallback backend + cache |
| 10 | `AttributeError: 'str' object has no attribute 'get'` in ad-hoc diagnostic | Annotation dict has non-int keys (e.g. `'prefix'`) | Iterate only dict-valued entries / filter keys |
| 11 | `find_unused_parameters=True` / `mt5→t5` / truncation warnings | Framework advisories | Harmless; left as-is |
| 12 | Large-epoch-count confusion during smoke tests | Smoke test used `--num-warmup-epochs 0`, producing degenerate output and loss 92 | Not a bug: with warmup the LLM reads unaligned tokens; full configs use warmup 50 |

